{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"syzygy syzygy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md","fileName":"Syzygy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Syzygy","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:15\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regular Sequences and Syzygies]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Syzygy Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"syzygy syzygy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md","fileName":"Syzygy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Syzygy","heading":"Syzygy","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A syzygy is a relation among generators f₁,…,fₜ of a module: a tuple (r₁,…,rₜ) such that r₁f₁ + ··· + rₜfₜ = 0.\n\nAll first syzygies form the [[Syzygy Module]]. Repeating the construction on generators of that module produces higher syzygies and the successive kernels in a free resolution.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Syzygy Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"syzygy syzygy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Syzygy.md","fileName":"Syzygy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Syzygy","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[commutativealgebra.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Syzygy Module","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}